# Chrome extension build configuration.
#
# Create .env.development.local / .env.production.local (both covered by the
# repo's .env.*.local gitignore rule — use these exact names). Never commit
# real environment values; development Clerk-instance identifiers in
# particular must stay out of the public repo.
#
# Values are strictly validated: KEY=VALUE lines only (no quotes), no unknown
# or duplicate keys, and URL values must be bare origins (scheme + host +
# port; a lone trailing slash is normalized away).
#
# Required in .env.development.local (dev Clerk instance values, no defaults):
#   CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   pk_test_… for the dev instance.
#   CLERK_FRONTEND_API      https://<instance>.clerk.accounts.dev
#
# Required in .env.production.local:
#   CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   pk_live_… (public by design, env-supplied by
#                           decision — see the migration plan's M7 step 0).
#
# Optional (defaults shown; production origins are PINNED — a differing
# override fails the build; add a distinct build mode instead):
#   TIDDLY_API_URL          development http://localhost:8000,
#                           production https://api.tiddly.me.
#   CLERK_SYNC_HOST         development http://localhost (Clerk's documented
#                           special case), production https://clerk.tiddly.me.
#   CLERK_FRONTEND_API      production default https://clerk.tiddly.me.
#
# Development http origins are allowed for loopback hosts only.
